P02.02.02 — replace the stub `workspace` gate with the QG-01 gate set and add `stress`.

This file is founder-only (protected-paths policy), so this session wrote the
change as a patch instead of editing it. Apply it yourself:

    git apply docs/control-plane/patches/0003-p02-gates.patch
    python3 .claude/bin/control_plane_check.py
    python3 .claude/bin/gates.py full

REVISED 2026-09-29. The first version of this patch was written before P02.07
moved the test runner: it used `pnpm turbo run test`, and turbo no longer owns a
`test` task, so applying it would have produced a config whose `unit` gate could
not run. Every command in this revision was executed individually against the
current tree before the patch was regenerated.

What changes
------------
Removed: the `workspace` stub (`pnpm turbo run lint typecheck test build`), which
existed only so `full` could not pass before P02 landed. It now fails for a
second reason too — turbo has no `test` task since P02.07.

Added, in QG-01's order (PLAN.md, Cross-Phase Quality Gates):

  conventions       Conventional Commit + no-attribution self-tests
  docs-consistency  ADR coverage, domain coverage, DFD coverage, threat-model
                    references, data classification
  format            prettier --check
  lint              turbo run lint
  boundaries        dependency-cruiser
  typecheck         turbo run typecheck
  unit              pnpm test  (vitest, unit project)
  integration       pnpm test:integration          [requires docker]
  migrations        expand/contract and lock safety
  build             turbo run build
  licences          production-dependency licence allowlist
  secret-scan       gitleaks over history, with the repository config

`fast` becomes control-plane, conventions, docs-consistency, format, lint,
typecheck, unit — the loop that needs no Docker.

`stress` is added (20 iterations of the unit project), which `gates.py stress`
needs and which the stub had no section for.

Not yet included, with the phase that adds them
-----------------------------------------------
  RLS catalog check + cross-tenant suite   P06.02, P06.03
  OpenAPI + client drift                   P06, P07

Each is a tightening, which needs no approval; they land with the phase that
makes them real rather than as a gate that passes because it checks nothing.

Notes
-----
`integration` requires Docker and the local environment file. Without them the
gate is reported SKIPPED-UNVERIFIED rather than passing, so a skip can never be
read as a pass.

The gate runner inherits whatever Node is on PATH. Run it under `nvm use` (Node
24.21.0); under Node 22 pnpm emits an unsupported-engine warning.

